                "text": "ISSUE_KIND: streetlight\nISSUE: Decorative double-arm streetlight with missing globes, exposed wiring, and an exposed bulb\nDETAILS: The photo shows a decorative double-arm streetlight against a bright blue daytime sky with the sun behind the center finial; both globes are missing, the left arm has exposed wiring with no bulb, and the right arm has a bare exposed bulb. The user note identifies pole number 86-112 and states that both lamps have been smashed since last Friday, leaving the block dark at night.\nORGANIZATION: New York City Department of Transportation (NYC DOT)\nDEPARTMENT: Division of Street Lighting\nWHY: West 86th Street at these coordinates in Manhattan is a public street inside the incorporated City of New York. NYC DOT maintains streetlights on all City roadways and pathways, including streets, through its Division of Street Lighting.\nCOVERAGE_QUOTE: \"NYC DOT maintains nearly 400,000 streetlights throughout New York City, and is a national leader in using sustainable street lighting.\"\nCOVERAGE_URL: https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEsWGF2uTvyEatkZ5eCt6EF17fyqsNm68K9Z2cIUnkST7hZPlsIpD_JezdjQ-2HUKwaHKMpKzs6ts3rWIwyWh3ge3mJJgdVnN0vZGbeaGsadBZJJwTFLich3GRsJ6W6kJ0rhZhHd4phhn7l50r5FGkFFZY65sj2-6_V\nREPORTING_URL: https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGKK2BX-d0_dOtzq8-k7KMKzmyJVDwRlpg8qdP58c2HhwFbQN7QFMhXSZlz8qzkfQuyERG6yTNeroBu-wfXFAK94YojCCbERNvscLOmHcQ6lCDcbHp8-tPe\nOFFICIAL_WEBSITE: https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEsWGF2uTvyEatkZ5eCt6EF17fyqsNm68K9Z2cIUnkST7hZPlsIpD_JezdjQ-2HUKwaHKMpKzs6ts3rWIwyWh3ge3mJJgdVnN0vZGbeaGsadBZJJwTFLich3GRsJ6W6kJ0rhZhHd4phhn7l50r5FGkFFZY65sj2-6_V\nEMAIL: StreetLighting@dot.nyc.gov | https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFq7-GSD9adblOSmvVgRlhysq_TPblNmHABSQEIyNLZ_FSrVYbiBc7ln-b2ohvwBt1S2TryCALC_dtnPFJUuAc7qpuQTX4gGwka-kqdW36lB-RqrERS3SvKbYWjLgaZgUm8VAXp9XAY8RDM806